<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1, wave 5 — the Twilight Deep's fishTypes binding
  (fish_bestiary_commission_2026-09-10.md §2D), the exact file the doc's own
  build sketch names (§5.2: "new ... BiomeFishTypes_TwilightDeep.xml under
  DEPLOY_HOLD.txt").

  🔴 HELD — see DEPLOY_HOLD.txt (deploy_custom_mods.py refuses to write this
  file to the live Mods folder) and RUT_TwilightFish_Niim.xml's own header
  for the full finding. Short version: `RUT_TwilightSea` is ONE BiomeDef for
  the ruled no-fish SURFACE and the fishable UNDER-ROOF deep water. Applying
  this patch today would make the surface fishable too — wrong per
  terminator_sea.md's own solitary-sea ruling. The under-roof water is not
  separable yet: no second BiomeDef exists for it, and the "diving-mods map
  layer" alternative the doc floated is MEASURED closed as of this wave —
  GravTide's dive maps (Biomes_Seabed.xml) are dry sea-FLOOR maps with
  maxFishPopulation 0 and no water on them at all, not a second open-water
  layer this water body's fishTypes could ever apply to. Resolving this for
  real needs a new BiomeDef (or map-generation layer) for the under-roof
  water plus a way for a colonist to reach it — biome/mechanism authoring,
  not a fish-item build. Filed as its own open question, not guessed at
  here: see FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1's wave 5 section.

  This patch is otherwise complete and correct against the doc's own table
  (§2D) and validates clean under validate_patch.py's def-checked mode — it
  resolves the right xpath against the right live def RIGHT NOW, same as any
  other patch.
  Only the DEPLOY_HOLD.txt entry stops it reaching the game. Lift the hold
  the moment the under-roof water gets its own def/layer; no other change to
  this file should be needed at that point beyond removing the hold entry.

  Values: saltwater_Common/_Uncommon exactly as §2D's table; maxFishPopulation
  700 — "high... against the Greentide's 720 as the ceiling, not above it"
  (the doc's own instruction), one economy-size population but not the
  largest on the planet. rareCatchesSetMaker -> RUT_RareTwilightCatches
  (RUT_RareTwilightCatches.xml, sibling, this wave).
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_TwilightSea"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <maxFishPopulation>700</maxFishPopulation>
      <fishTypes MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
        <saltwater_Common>
          <RUT_Niim>1.5</RUT_Niim>
          <RUT_Pallu>1</RUT_Pallu>
          <RUT_Tikkarr>0.8</RUT_Tikkarr>
          <RUT_Nuudal>0.6</RUT_Nuudal>
        </saltwater_Common>
        <saltwater_Uncommon>
          <RUT_Kellu>1</RUT_Kellu>
          <RUT_Murrol>0.8</RUT_Murrol>
          <RUT_Hollu>0.8</RUT_Hollu>
          <RUT_Oobo>0.4</RUT_Oobo>
        </saltwater_Uncommon>
        <rareCatchesSetMaker>RUT_RareTwilightCatches</rareCatchesSetMaker>
      </fishTypes>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
